# Build context: the repository root (docker build -f Model-Pipeline/Dockerfile .).
#
# An allowlist: everything is left out, then only what the image needs is let back in. A local
# checkout can hold comment text (Model-Pipeline/data/, Data-Pipeline/data/raw, drift batches),
# key files under any name, and outputs; none of it can reach the image, whatever it is called.
# src.pipeline.container_check also fails the CI build if any file in the image is not tracked
# by git. Building from a clean checkout (CI, or `git archive`) is still the safest.
*

!.git
!.dvc
!.dvcignore
!.gitignore

!Model-Pipeline/src
!Model-Pipeline/configs
!Model-Pipeline/artifacts
!Model-Pipeline/tests
!Model-Pipeline/pyproject.toml
!Model-Pipeline/requirements*.txt

# The id lists and the obfuscation script the evaluation tables are built with.
!Data-Pipeline/data/splits
!Data-Pipeline/data/*.dvc
!Data-Pipeline/scripts
!Data-Pipeline/config

# Inside what was let back in: DVC's local state, caches, and any key file.
.dvc/cache
.dvc/tmp
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
**/*.key.json
**/*service-account*.json
**/*credentials*.json
# GCP's default key file name: <project>-<12 hex digits>.json
**/*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].json
